export const REFERENCE = "Weft is a JavaScript API for FPGA hardware. A script is the body of a function that returns design(…). Builder lambdas (B) run now in JS; hardware lambdas (H) are parsed into the IR and never called, so they see only $, the prelude, params and what .lib() ships; runtime lambdas (R) run later beside the simulator or the board.\n\nEvery form used in F-01 through F-19, grouped by what it builds, with the example that introduces it. The \"Lambda\" column says which kind a function argument is: B builder (runs now), H hardware (parsed), R runtime (runs beside the simulator or board).\n## Grammar · Types and the hardware prelude\n  bit, u(n), s(n)\n      One bit; n-bit unsigned; n-bit two's complement · F-01, F-02\n  pulse\n      A bit that returns to 0 on cycles that do not write it · F-02\n  vec(T, n), struct({ … })\n      Arrays and records of types · F-04, F-05\n  T.init(v)\n      The register's reset value · F-04\n  wrap(x, T?), sat(x, T)\n      Narrow by keeping low bits; narrow by clamping · H · F-02, F-08\n  x[i], x.bits(hi, lo), x.as(T)\n      One bit; a bit range; reinterpret the same bits · H · F-06, F-08, F-17\n  clog2(k)\n      Bits needed to count k values · B, H · F-11\n  past(x), within(n, x), sequence(…)\n      Temporal helpers for properties · H · F-11\n## Grammar · Modules, fsms and pipelines\n  module(name), fsm(name), pipeline(name)\n      A component; fsm and pipeline add their own methods · F-01, F-06, F-09\n  .in(name, T), .out(name, T), or an object of them\n      Ports; a type may be a lambda of params · B · F-02, F-04\n  .regs({ … })\n      Internal registers · B · F-03\n  .seq(fn), .every(dur, fn), .on(event, fn)\n      Clocked blocks: what they write is a register · H · F-02, F-01, F-05\n  .comb(fn)\n      A combinational block: what it writes is a wire · H · F-02\n  .params({ … }), .require(fn)\n      Build-time parameters and a check on them · B · F-04, F-11\n  .with({ … }), .as(name), .domain(name)\n      A new specialized, renamed or re-clocked value · F-04, F-18\n  .lib({ … } | fn)\n      Ship constants, tables and helpers into hardware lambdas · B · F-03, F-06\n  .provides(…), .needs(…)\n      Streams produced and consumed, linked by name · F-05\n  .bind({ port: resource })\n      Claim a board resource for a port · F-01\n  .ram(name, { of, words })\n      A memory owned by the module · F-08\n  .knob(name, T, { reset, min, max }), .status(name, T), .irq(name)\n      Registers the host may turn, may read, or hears from · F-12\n  .budget(fn), .hint(fn), .pipelined({ path })\n      Resource limits, mapping hints, latency the compiler may change · B · F-03, F-15\n  .assert(name, fn), .assume(name, fn), .cover(name, fn)\n      Properties for simulation, proofs and monitors · H · F-11\n  .supervise(fn), .probe(fn)\n      Watchdog with local reset; on-chip signal capture · B (watchdog condition H) · F-19\n  .migrate(fn)\n      Map old register values to new ones on a live swap · R · F-17\n  fsm: .initial(s), .state(s, fn), .step(stream), .encode(kind)\n      States as lambdas returning the next state · H · F-06, F-19\n  pipeline: .stage(name, fn), .stall(kind)\n      Stages with inferred pipeline registers · H · F-09\n  In hardware: $.x, $.push(s, v), $.has(s), $.take(s), $.mem.read(a), $.mem.q, $.mem.write(a, v)\n      Signals, stream beats and memory ports · H · F-01 to F-08\n## Grammar · Streams, memories and standard parts\n  stream(name).of(T)\n      A typed valid/ready channel · F-06\n  .buffer(n, { overflow })\n      Depth and policy: block, drop-oldest, drop-newest, latest · F-07\n  .cross({ from, to })\n      A sanctioned clock-domain crossing · F-10\n  rom(name).of(T).from(n, i => v)\n      A table filled by a builder lambda · F-08\n  std.debounce, std.uart.rx, std.uart.tx, std.sigmaDelta, std.video.timing, std.video.hdmi, std.bridge.uart\n      Standard components, configured with their own methods · F-05 to F-19\n## Grammar · Designs\n  design(name), .use(…)\n      The top level and what it contains · F-01\n  .board(profile), .boards({ … }), .part(name), board(p).part(name)\n      Where it runs: one board, several, or a bare part · F-01, F-13, F-16\n  .clocks(c => c.pin(…).pll(…).port(…))\n      Clock domains and how each is made · F-10, F-13\n  .wire(a, b), .wire([[a, b], …]), .pins({ … })\n      Explicit connections and pin bindings · F-02, F-04\n  group(name).children(…).supervise(…)\n      A reset group with a restart strategy · F-19\n  .boot(b => b.start(…).then(…).background(…))\n      The order in which resets are released · F-19\n  .regions(…), .place({ … }), .record({ … })\n      Reconfigurable slots, what lives in them, what is recorded for replay · F-17\n  .prove(p => p.module(…).bmc(k).induction().engine(…))\n      Formal proofs · F-11\n  .scenario(name, fn, { levels, targets })\n      A test, run at chosen IR levels and targets · F-01, F-14, F-16\n## Grammar · The compiler\n  .compile(c => …)\n      Configure the pass pipeline; with nothing, the default runs · F-08\n  c.use(p), c.stage(name, s => s.pass(…).fixpoint(…))\n      Start from a pipeline; declare a stage · F-13\n  c.after(x, …), c.before(x, …), c.replace(x, p), c.when(t => …, …)\n      Edit a pipeline, per target if needed · F-14, F-15, F-16\n  c.cache(dir), c.verifyEach(), c.snapshot(…), c.inspect(…), c.explainPlan()\n      Incremental builds and seeing inside · F-13, F-14\n  c.check(name, r => true | message), c.emit(backend, opts)\n      Checks on the report; outputs · F-08, F-12\n  c.explore(x => x.knob(…).measure(…).keep(…).pareto(…))\n      Design-space exploration · F-15\n  pass(name).on(level).requires(…).preserves(…).params(…).visit(op, fn)\n      A transformation (fn is B, over the IR) · F-14\n  analysis(name).on(level).run(fn)\n      A cached fact about the IR · F-14\n  rewrite(name).from(fn).where(fn).to(fn).examples(…)\n      A rule: pattern and replacement are H, the guard is B · F-14\n  backend(name).on(level).emit((ir, out) => …)\n      An output written by walking an IR level · F-16\n## Grammar · Scenarios, runtime, changes and agents\n  sc.wait, .step, .poke, .press, .toggle, .uart, .feed, .throttle, .write, .hang, .repeat\n      Drive the simulated design · F-01 to F-19\n  sc.expectPins, .expectSignal, .expectState, .expectStream, .expectUart, .expectFrame, .expectDropped, .expectKnob, .expectIrq, .expectResets, .expectToggles\n      Check it; their lambdas are R · F-01 to F-19\n  async tb => … with tb.poke, tb.peek, tb.push, tb.pull, tb.random, tb.expect, tb.expectCoverage\n      An imperative testbench · F-03, F-09, F-11\n  host(name).over(bridge).onStart(fn).every(dur, fn).on(event, fn) with dev.knob(p).set/update, dev.status(p).read\n      Software beside the board · F-12, F-19\n  change(title).knob(…).patch(…).replace(…)\n      A change to the running design · F-17\n  .verify(v => …), .deploy(d => d.partial(…).canary(…)), .rollbackOn(…)\n      How it is checked, loaded and undone · F-17\n  sc.apply, .approve, .build, .expectChange, .expectBuild, .expectProposal, .expectEscalation\n      Drive and check the change pipeline · F-17 to F-19\n  agent(name).model(…).guidelines(…).scope(…).budget(…).on(event, fn), std.agents.mechanic\n      A participant that proposes changes · F-18, F-19\n\nThe API as typed declarations, the IR's opcodes, the pass catalogue and the diagnostics. The declarations are TypeScript notation for reference only; the implementation is JavaScript. HW marks a hardware lambda (parsed, never called) and RT a runtime lambda.\n\n## API declarations\n// ---- types and lambdas ----\ninterface Type { readonly width: number; readonly signed: boolean; init(v: number | bigint | object): Type }\ndeclare function u(n: number): Type;           declare function s(n: number): Type;\ndeclare const bit: Type, pulse: Type;\ndeclare function vec(t: Type, n: number): Type; declare function struct(f: Record<string, Type>): Type;\ntype Params = Record<string, unknown>;\ntype Env = { clock: { name: string; hz: number }; part: string; board?: string };\ntype Lazy<T> = T | ((p: Params, env: Env) => T);       // a builder lambda of params (D2, D3)\ntype HW = ($: any, ...args: any[]) => any;             // parsed into HIR, never called\ntype RT<A extends any[], R> = (...a: A) => R;           // ordinary JS, runs beside sim or board\ntype Dur = string;                                      // \"250ms\", \"1s\", \"48 kHz\"\n\n// ---- components: module(), fsm(), pipeline() ----\ninterface Component<Self> {\n  readonly name: string;\n  params(p: Params): Self;                 require(check: (p: Params) => true | string): Self;\n  in(name: string, t: Lazy<Type>): Self;   in(ports: Record<string, Lazy<Type>>): Self;\n  out(name: string, t: Lazy<Type>): Self;  out(ports: Record<string, Lazy<Type>>): Self;\n  regs(r: Lazy<Record<string, Type>>): Self;\n  seq(f: HW): Self;  comb(f: HW): Self;  every(d: Dur, f: HW): Self;\n  on(event: string, f: HW): Self;          // a stream name, \"port.rise\" or \"port.fall\"\n  provides(...streams: string[]): Self;    needs(...streams: string[]): Self;\n  lib(v: Lazy<Record<string, unknown>>): Self;\n  bind(m: Record<string, string>): Self;   domain(name: string): Self;\n  ram(name: string, o: { of: Type; words: number; rdw?: \"read-first\" | \"write-first\" }): Self;\n  knob(name: string, t: Type, o?: { reset?: number; min?: number; max?: number; doc?: string }): Self;\n  status(name: string, t: Type): Self;     irq(name: string): Self;\n  budget(f: (b: Budget) => Budget): Self;  hint(h: Lazy<Record<string, string>>): Self;\n  pipelined(o: { path: [string, string] }): Self;\n  assert(name: string, f: HW): Self;  assume(name: string, f: HW): Self;  cover(name: string, f: HW): Self;\n  supervise(f: (s: Supervisor) => Supervisor): Self;  probe(f: (p: Probe) => Probe): Self;\n  migrate(f: RT<[Record<string, number>], Record<string, number>>): Self;\n  with(p: Params): Self;  as(name: string): Self;\n}\ninterface Fsm extends Component<Fsm> {\n  initial(s: string): Fsm;  state(s: string, f: HW): Fsm;  step(stream: string): Fsm;\n  encode(e: \"auto\" | \"binary\" | \"onehot\" | \"gray\"): Fsm;\n}\ninterface Pipeline extends Component<Pipeline> { stage(name: string, f: HW): Pipeline; stall(k: \"global\" | \"skid\"): Pipeline }\ninterface Budget { luts(n: number): Budget; ffs(n: number): Budget; brams(n: number): Budget; dsps(n: number): Budget }\ninterface Supervisor { watchdog(d: Dur, alive: HW): Supervisor; reset(k: \"local\"): Supervisor;\n  strategy(k: \"one-for-one\" | \"all-for-one\" | \"dependents\"): Supervisor; maxResets(n: number, window: Dur): Supervisor; escalate(agent: string): Supervisor }\ninterface Probe { signals(...names: string[]): Probe; depth(n: number): Probe; keep(k: \"before-reset\" | \"on-trigger\"): Probe }\n\n// ---- streams, memories, groups ----\ninterface Stream { of(t: Type): Stream; buffer(n: number, o?: { overflow: \"block\" | \"drop-oldest\" | \"drop-newest\" | \"latest\" }): Stream;\n  cross(o: { from: string; to: string }): Stream }\ninterface Rom { of(t: Type): Rom; from(n: number, f: (i: number) => number): Rom }\ninterface Group { children(...names: string[]): Group; supervise(f: (s: Supervisor) => Supervisor): Group }\n\n// ---- designs ----\ntype Level = \"hir\" | \"dag\" | \"net\" | \"phys\";\ninterface Design {\n  board(b: string | Board): Design;  boards(m: Record<string, Board>): Design;  part(p: string): Design;\n  clocks(f: (c: Clocks) => Clocks): Design;\n  use(...items: unknown[]): Design;\n  wire(from: string, to: string): Design;  wire(pairs: [string, string][]): Design;  pins(m: Record<string, string>): Design;\n  regions(f: (r: Regions) => Regions): Design;  place(m: Record<string, string>): Design;\n  record(o: { streams?: string[]; inputs?: boolean; keep: Dur }): Design;\n  boot(f: (b: Boot) => Boot): Design;\n  compile(f?: (c: Compiler) => Compiler): Design;\n  prove(f: (p: Prover) => Prover): Design;\n  scenario(name: string, f: ((sc: Sc) => Sc) | RT<[Tb], Promise<void>>, o?: { levels?: Level[]; targets?: \"all\" | string[] }): Design;\n}\ninterface Board { part(p: string): Board }\ninterface Clocks { pin(name: string, resource: string): Clocks; port(name: string, o: { hz: string }): Clocks;\n  pll(name: string, o: { from: string; hz: string; tolerance?: string }): Clocks }\ninterface Boot { start(...g: string[]): Boot; then(...g: string[]): Boot; background(...g: string[]): Boot }\ninterface Prover { module(name: string): Prover; bmc(k: number): Prover; induction(): Prover; engine(e: \"smt\" | \"abc-pdr\"): Prover }\n\n// ---- the compiler ----\ninterface Compiler {\n  use(p: PassPipeline): Compiler;  stage(name: string, f: (s: Stage) => Stage): Compiler;\n  after(at: string, f: (s: Stage) => Stage): Compiler;  before(at: string, f: (s: Stage) => Stage): Compiler;\n  replace(name: string, p: Pass): Compiler;  without(name: string): Compiler;\n  when(pred: (t: Target) => boolean, f: (c: Compiler) => Compiler): Compiler;\n  cache(dir: string): Compiler;  verifyEach(): Compiler;  validate(o?: { passes?: string[] }): Compiler;   // validate: D10\n  snapshot(l: Level, o: { after: string; as: \"dot\" | \"text\" | \"json\"; to: string }): Compiler;\n  inspect(l: Level, f: (ir: IR) => void, o?: { after: string }): Compiler;\n  check(name: string, f: (r: Report, t: Target) => true | string): Compiler;\n  emit(b: string | Backend, o?: { to?: string | ((t: Target) => string); level?: Level }): Compiler;\n  explore(f: (x: Explorer) => Explorer): Compiler;  explainPlan(): Compiler;\n}\ninterface Stage { pass(...p: Pass[]): Stage; fixpoint(o: { max: number }): Stage }\ninterface PassB { on(l: Level): PassB; requires(...a: Array<Analysis | string>): PassB; preserves(...names: string[]): PassB;\n  params(p: Params): PassB; visit(op: string | string[], f: (n: Node, g: IR, ctx: Record<string, unknown>) => void): PassB;\n  run(f: (g: IR, ctx: Record<string, unknown>) => void): PassB; readonly(): PassB; with(p: Params): PassB }\ninterface AnalysisB { on(l: Level): AnalysisB; run(f: (g: IR) => unknown): AnalysisB }\ninterface RewriteB { from(p: HW): RewriteB; where(f: (m: Record<string, Node>) => boolean): RewriteB; to(r: HW): RewriteB;\n  examples(e: Array<[HW, HW | null]>): RewriteB }\ninterface BackendB { on(l: Level): BackendB; emit(f: (ir: IR, out: { file(path: string, text: string): void }) => void): BackendB }\ninterface Explorer { knob(path: string, values: unknown[]): Explorer; measure(f: (r: Report) => Record<string, unknown>): Explorer;\n  keep(f: (m: Record<string, unknown>) => boolean): Explorer; pareto(keys: string[]): Explorer; parallel(n: number): Explorer; report(path: string): Explorer }\n\n// ---- runtime, changes, agents ----\ninterface Tb { poke(path: string, v: number): Promise<void>; peek(path: string): Promise<number>; step(n?: number): Promise<void>;\n  wait(d: Dur): Promise<void>; set(pins: string, v: number): Promise<void>; measure(pin: string, o: { over: Dur }): Promise<number>;\n  push(stream: string, beats: unknown | unknown[]): Promise<void>; pull(stream: string, n?: number): Promise<unknown>;\n  random: { int(lo: number, hi: number): number }; expect(c: boolean, msg?: string): void;\n  expectEqual(a: unknown, b: unknown, msg?: string): void; expectCoverage(k: \"all\" | string[]): void }\ninterface Host { over(bridge: string): Host; onStart(f: RT<[Dev], unknown>): Host; every(d: Dur, f: RT<[Dev], unknown>): Host;\n  on(event: string, f: RT<[Dev, unknown], unknown>): Host }\ninterface Dev { knob(path: string): { get(): Promise<number>; set(v: number): Promise<void>; update(f: (v: number) => number): Promise<void> };\n  status(path: string): { read(): Promise<number> }; registers(): Promise<unknown>; clock: { seconds(): number }; log(...a: unknown[]): void }\ninterface Change { knob(path: string, v: number): Change; patch(module: string, p: { lib?: Record<string, unknown>; on?: Record<string, HW>; seq?: HW; comb?: HW }): Change;\n  replace(module: string, m: Component<any>): Change; verify(f: (v: Verify) => Verify): Change;\n  deploy(f: (d: Deploy) => Deploy): Change; rollbackOn(...events: Array<\"assert\" | \"stall\" | \"watchdog\" | \"timing\">): Change }\ninterface Verify { lint(): Verify; ports(k: \"same\"): Verify; replay(window: string): Verify; timing(): Verify; equiv(o?: { upTo?: \"stream latency\" }): Verify }\ninterface Deploy { partial(region: string): Deploy; canary(d: Dur, o?: { watch: string[] }): Deploy }\ninterface Agent { model(m: string): Agent; guidelines(t: string): Agent; scope(f: (s: Scope) => Scope): Agent;\n  budget(o: { proposals: number; per: string }): Agent; on(event: string, f: RT<[Ctx, unknown], unknown>): Agent }\n\n## IR opcodes\n  in\n      the port's type · Value of an input port this cycle\n  out\n      x · the port's type · Drives an output port\n  const\n      narrowest type (D1), or attrs.type · A literal; attrs.value is a BigInt, and attrs.type keeps a declared type when folding produced the constant\n  reg\n      —; next set separately · declared type · Q of a register; attrs.init, domain; next is its D input\n  add, sub\n      a, b · D1 · Exact sum or difference; cannot overflow its own type\n  mul\n      a, b · w_a + w_b bits · Exact product\n  neg\n      a · s(n + 1) · Exact negation\n  and, or, xor\n      a, b · the wider operand · Bitwise, after extension\n  not\n      a · same · Bitwise inversion\n  shl, shr, ashr\n      a, k · constant k: w ± k; dynamic k: shl w + 2^w_k − 1, shr w · Shifts; ashr keeps the sign\n  eq, ne, lt, le, gt, ge\n      a, b · bit · Comparisons; attrs.signed\n  mux\n      c, t, f · smallest type holding t and f · c ? t : f\n  concat\n      a, b, … · sum of widths · The first operand is most significant\n  slice\n      a · hi − lo + 1 bits · Bits hi..lo; wrap() lowers to it\n  sext, zext\n      a · attrs.width · Sign or zero extension\n  sat\n      a · target type · Clamp to the target's range\n  mem\n      One memory; attrs.words, rdw, init\n  memrd\n      mem, addr, en · element type · Read port; the address is registered inside the port and the data appears on the next cycle (D8)\n  memwr\n      mem, addr, data, en · Write port; writes at the edge when en is high\n  rom\n      index · element type · Combinational table read; attrs.table, type\n  cell\n      inputs · attrs.outputs · A technology cell at level net: LUT, FF, CARRY, DSP, RAM\n  probe\n      x, … · Marks signals for scenarios and on-chip capture\nPure opcodes are hash-consed on (op, args, type, attrs). in, out, reg, mem, memrd, memwr and probe are never merged.\n\n## Pass catalogue\n  parse\n      front · source → hir · Parses hardware lambdas; runs the capture check (D2)\n  elaborate\n      front · hir · Applies params, .with(), .require(); memoizes specializations (D3)\n  link\n      front · hir · Joins provides/needs, .wire() and pins; inserts forks; reports unmet-need, multi-producer, pin-claimed\n  fsm.extract\n      lower · hir · States and returns → transition graph and next-state logic\n  pipeline.registers\n      lower · hir · Inserts registers for values live across stages\n  stream.lower\n      lower · hir · Handshakes, buffers by depth and policy, drop counters (D7)\n  csr.collect\n      lower · hir · Gathers knobs, status and irqs into one register map and a bus slave\n  flatten\n      lower · hir → dag · Merges blocks (D4), removes hierarchy, one DAG per domain\n  widths\n      lower · dag · Infers and enforces D1\n  checks.loops\n      lower · dag · Rejects combinational cycles (comb-loop)\n  checks.latches\n      lower · dag · Rejects wires not assigned on every path (latch)\n  checks.cdc\n      lower · dag · Propagates domains; rejects unmarked crossings (cdc)\n  constFold\n      optimize · dag · Evaluates nodes whose operands are constants\n  cse\n      optimize · dag · Merges structurally equal pure nodes\n  muxTree\n      optimize · dag · Flattens and simplifies nested multiplexers\n  dce\n      optimize · dag · Removes nodes that reach no output, register or probe; narrows unused high bits\n  pipeline.cut\n      time · dag · Places pipeline stages on .pipelined() paths to meet the clock\n  retime\n      time · dag · Moves registers on .pipelined() paths (Leiserson–Saxe)\n  mem.infer\n      map · dag → net · Maps memories and registered ROM reads to RAM cells (D8)\n  dsp.pack\n      map · dag → net · Folds multiply, add and register into DSP cells\n  fsm.encode\n      map · dag · Chooses state encodings (D12)\n  srl.infer\n      map · net · 7-series only: shift-register chains to SRL16/SRL32 cells\n  techmap\n      map · dag → net · Maps logic to the part's LUTs and carry chains\n  place\n      back · net → phys · Assigns each cell a site\n  route\n      back · phys · Assigns each net a path\n  timing\n      back · phys · Static timing analysis; error timing on negative slack\n\n## Diagnostics\n  capture\n      error · parse · A hardware lambda uses a name outside $, the prelude, params and .lib()\n  lib-shadows-param\n      error · parse · A .lib() name equals a parameter name\n  lib-value\n      error · parse · A shipped value has no hardware meaning (a Map, a class instance)\n  unroll-bound\n      error · parse · A loop bound is not constant, or exceeds 4096 iterations\n  temporal-position\n      error · parse · within() or sequence() used outside the positions R9.2 allows\n  mem-read-value\n      error · parse · $.m.read(a) used as an expression; read data arrives in $.m.q on the next cycle\n  require\n      error · elaborate · A .require() check returned a message\n  unmet-need\n      error · link · A needed stream has no producer\n  multi-producer\n      error · link · Two modules provide one stream\n  pin-claimed\n      error · link · Two modules bind one output resource\n  fsm-target\n      error · fsm.extract · An initial or returned state is not a declared state\n  fsm-unreachable\n      warning · fsm.extract · A state cannot be reached from the initial state\n  every-no-clock\n      error · lower · .every() in a domain without a known frequency\n  width\n      error · widths · A narrowing assignment without wrap() or sat()\n  rom-index\n      error · widths · A ROM index type is wider than ⌈log2 n⌉ bits for an n-entry table\n  mixed-kind\n      error · flatten · A signal written in a clocked block and in .comb\n  multi-driver\n      error · flatten · Two .comb blocks write one wire\n  multi-writer\n      warning · flatten · Two clocked blocks can write one register on the same cycle; a witness is shown\n  mem-ports\n      error · flatten · Two reads or two writes of one .ram() can happen on the same cycle; a witness is shown\n  comb-read-before-write\n      error · flatten · A .comb lambda reads a wire before writing it\n  latch\n      error · checks.latches · A wire is not assigned on every path\n  comb-loop\n      error · checks.loops · A cycle without a register\n  cdc\n      error · checks.cdc · A signal crosses domains without .cross() or a crossing cell\n  pll\n      error · lower · No PLL or MMCM setting meets every requested output of one PLL within tolerance and VCO limits\n  region\n      error · lower · A raw wire crosses a reconfigurable region's boundary; only streams and knobs may (R15.5)\n  record-budget\n      error · map · A .record() window does not fit the board's memory or host link (R15.7)\n  rule-unsound\n      error · rewrite engine · A rewrite rule fails its proof at some width (D10)\n  lint\n      warning · a readonly pass · A message from g.warn(), reported at the node's source line\n  budget\n      error · map · A module exceeds its .budget()\n  timing\n      error · timing · Negative slack after routing; the path is reported by source line\n  stream-protocol\n      error · simulation · Valid fell, or data changed, before a beat fired (D7)\n  assert\n      error · simulation, proof · An assertion failed; the trace or counterexample is attached\n  assume-violated\n      error · simulation · The stimulus broke an assumption: a testbench bug, not a design bug\n  vacuous\n      warning · proof · No run satisfies the assumptions to the requested depth, so every assertion holds trivially\n";
export const GUIDELINES = "You are the architect in Weft Lab, a browser IDE for Weft: a JavaScript API for designing FPGA hardware. The user edits a script (the body of a function that returns design(…)); the Lab compiles it through a multi-pass compiler to one dataflow DAG per clock domain, simulates it cycle by cycle on a virtual board, runs its scenarios, proves its properties, estimates resources and timing, and applies changes to the running design through a change pipeline.\n\nHow to work\n- Look before you change. Read the script with editor.get(), the diagnostics with editor.check(), and the state of the board with io.* and report(). Say what you found in a sentence or two.\n- Make the smallest edit that does the job, with editor.edit(find, replace), and check its diagnostics. Keep the file's header comment (/** F-NN Title … */) and its style: short lines, builders chained one per line, a comment where a reader would stop.\n- Prove it works. Boot it (editor.boot({ run: \"50ms\" })), drive the board (io.press, io.toggle, io.uart), read pins, registers and streams, and run the scenarios (scenarios.runAll()). Add a scenario when you add behaviour.\n- Report evidence, not hope: a table (chat.table), a register value, a scenario result, the slack from report(). Link to lines as [line 12](lab:line?n=12) and to tabs as [Waves](lab:tab?name=waves).\n- Stop when the change works or when you need a decision from the user. Never loop on the same failing step: explain what blocks you.\n\nThe grammar's three kinds of lambda\n- Builder lambdas run now, in JS, while the script is evaluated: they compute tables, widths and parameters.\n- Hardware lambdas ($ => …) are parsed into the IR and never called. They see only $, their arguments, the hardware prelude (u, s, bit, pulse, wrap, sat, clog2, past, within, …), the module's params and what .lib() ships. Using any other JS variable is a `capture` error: ship it with .lib({ NAME }).\n- Runtime lambdas (host(), scenario checks, .migrate(), agent handlers) are ordinary JS that runs beside the simulator or the board.\n\nHardware facts that matter\n- Widths grow (D1): u8 + u8 is u9, u8 - u8 is s9, a product is the sum of the widths. Putting a wider value into a narrower register needs wrap() or sat(); compound assignments (+=, -=) wrap by definition.\n- What a clocked block (.seq, .every, .on) writes is a register; what .comb writes is a wire that must be assigned on every path.\n- Streams are valid/ready channels linked by name (.provides / .needs). A beat fires when valid and ready are both high. Buffers choose a policy: block, drop-oldest, drop-newest, latest.\n- RAM reads take a cycle: $.mem.read(a) now, $.mem.q on the next cycle.\n- Signals crossing clock domains need stream(…).cross() or a crossing cell; otherwise checks.cdc refuses the build.\n- Knobs (.knob) are registers the host may write at runtime, clamped to [min, max] in hardware; changing one is a register write, not a rebuild.\n- Timing is estimated from a per-family delay model: deep adder trees, wide multiplies and long mux chains are the usual critical paths. Fixes: .pipelined() on a stream path, a ROM instead of logic, narrower types, or fewer levels.\n\nThe board\n- pico: iCE40 UP5K, 12 MHz, led:0..2, btn:user, uart. dev: Artix-7 xc7a35t, 100 MHz, led:0..7, btn:0..3, sw:0..7, uart, hdmi, audio. studio: like dev with btn:up, btn:down, btn:a, btn:b.\n- Simulated time is in picoseconds. A 100 MHz domain runs 100,000 cycles per simulated millisecond; run in milliseconds, not seconds, unless the design is slow.\n\nChanges to a running design\n- Apply ▸ (editor.apply) and changes.submit send a change through proposed → checked → verified → built → canary → committed, or rolled back when an assert trips during the canary. A knob-only change commits at once. Changes that wait for approval stay in the Changes tab: tell the user, do not approve them yourself unless asked.\n";
